Aim

To study how an insurance company manages customer leads using digital marketing techniques.

Beginner Level Exact Steps
Step 1: Open Browser

Open Google Chrome.

Step 2: Open Insurance Company Website

Open any insurance company website.

Examples:

LIC India
PolicyBazaar
Step 3: Observe Customer Inquiry Process

On homepage observe:

Contact forms
Policy enquiry
Quote request
Customer support
Step 4: Fill Sample Inquiry Form

Enter sample details:

Name
Mobile number
Email
Insurance type

Example:

Field	Example
Name	Ravi
Insurance Type	Health Insurance

Do not submit real personal information unnecessarily.

Step 5: Study Lead Collection Process

Understand how company collects customer leads from:

Website forms
Social media ads
Email campaigns
Mobile apps
Step 6: Study CRM Usage

Read about CRM (Customer Relationship Management).

Insurance companies use CRM to:

Store customer details
Track leads
Follow customer status
Manage communication
Step 7: Observe Follow-Up Methods

Companies contact customers through:

Phone calls
SMS
Emails
WhatsApp messages
Step 8: Study Lead Conversion

Observe how leads become customers.

Example Process:

Customer visits website
Fills inquiry form
Company contacts customer
Policy details explained
Customer buys insurance policy
Step 9: Prepare Simple Flow Diagram
Customer Visit → Inquiry Form → CRM Storage → Follow-Up → Policy Purchase
Step 10: Write Advantages
Advantages of Lead Management
Better customer tracking
Faster response
Improved sales
Organized customer data
Better communication
Step 11: Create Report in MS Word

Type:

Aim
Procedure
Lead management process
Advantages
Conclusion

Save as:

InsuranceLeadManagement.docx
Step 12: Take Screenshots

Take screenshots of:

Insurance website
Inquiry forms
CRM explanation pages

